title: What happens when the shell runs ls
actor sh: shell
actor k: kernel
actor ch: child process with a long name
actor fs: file system
sh -> k: `fork()`
k -> ch: create
note over ch: a copy of the shell,\nsame code
ch -> k: `exec("ls")`
k -> fs: load ls
fs ..> k: program bytes
ch -> ch: run ls
ch ..> sh: exit status
note over sh,k: the shell waits
